From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] test: use supported Check assertions without extra format args
Origin: downstream, based on upstream issue 2887 and Check 0.15.2 public API
Bug: https://bugs.netsurf-browser.org/mantis/view.php?id=2887
Upstream-Status: Not submitted; existing upstream report remains open
License: MIT

Check 0.15.2 appends NULL to deprecated fail_unless, provoking GCC's
format-extra-args diagnostic. Use ck_assert for no-message assertions and
ck_assert_msg otherwise. Conditions, messages, registration and expected
signals are unchanged; do not suppress warnings or skip any original test.
Remove when a released upstream version ports these assertions.

